From xenophon at irtnog.org  Tue Feb 22 14:52:27 2005
From: xenophon at irtnog.org (Matthew X. Economou)
Date: Tue Feb 22 14:52:29 2005
Subject: kernel panic on AS1000a
Message-ID: <B9638CACBA387E48927BB56B6A1555076AA5@svr1.irtnog.org>

Tom,
 
I reported the same problem in bug report http://www.freebsd.org/cgi/query-pr.cgi?pr=61940.  Basically, you can work around the problem by using the FreeBSD/alpha 4.11-RELEASE installation or mini-installation CD to format the device.
 
Versions prior to 5.3-RELEASE do not correctly support the Mylex DAC960 (KZPSC) array controller.  I have 5.3-RELEASE installed and running properly on an AS2000 with a RAID-5 array hosted by the KZPSC controller.
 
Best wishes,
Matthew
